  "base_repo_coverage": {
    "note": "Which signers a family ships in its base repositories, from anchored directory listings read 2026-09-16. This decides whether an OS release could deliver a signer default at all.",
    "observations": [
      {"repo": "CentOS 7.9 base (RHEL 7)", "bind": "9.11.4", "knot": "absent", "pdns": "absent"},
      {"repo": "Rocky 8.5 AppStream (RHEL 8)", "bind": "9.11.26", "knot": "absent", "pdns": "absent"},
      {"repo": "Rocky 9 AppStream (RHEL 9)", "bind": "9.16.23", "knot": "absent", "pdns": "absent"},
      {"repo": "EPEL 9", "bind": "absent", "knot": "3.3.10", "pdns": "5.0.7"}
    ],
    "consequence": "On RHEL and its rebuilds the only base-repo signer is BIND, and BIND gained an ECDSA-default policy in 9.16, which reached that family with RHEL 9 on 2022-05-17. Knot and PowerDNS require EPEL. An operator on this family could not receive an ECDSA signing default through the OS before 2022."
  },
